  "conclusions": [
    "The live cache uses combinational multiple reads and same-cycle guard/update ownership checks; direct conversion to synchronous BRAM/URAM changes cycle semantics and is not admitted.",
    "Address histogram has parallel updates across many slots in one target cycle, while all ports and exact same-cycle arithmetic must remain; one BRAM cannot replace it directly.",
    "FPGA implementation sharing of decodes/one-hot muxes is admissible only with full-width and cycle equivalence; no narrowing/token dropping or serializing target updates.",
    "MSHR0 mapped net names include DCache lineGeneration/slotEpoch/imageKey logic: mapped hierarchy alone cannot identify a source-local MSHR fix.",
    "Read counts are source expression lines, not independently proven physical ports; source lines and synthesized net cones must both be checked before a storage redesign."
  ],
